WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:08.590
As we get into the dog days of the summer
I wanna get you guys up to speed on some behind

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:12.890
the scenes happenings, as well as tell you
a bit about my plans for the near future.

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:17.830
Before I do that, I quickly want to address
my conversation with Patreon CEO Jack Conte

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:19.170
from earlier this week.

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:23.470
I think this chat, as much as any we've had
here, gets to the heart of what I've tried

00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:26.140
to do with The Rubin Report for the past two
years.

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:30.160
Jack and I had an honest conversation about
new media, economics and personal liberty

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:34.430
and couched around the issue I care most about,
free speech.

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:38.660
I hope whether you came away from the interview
agreeing with Jack or not, you got a better

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:44.960
understanding of the complexities and contradictions
we all face whether you are a creator, a CEO,

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:47.550
or a supporter of online content.

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:51.580
As I've mentioned time and time again, I believe
vital it is to occasionally put down your

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:55.470
phone, disconnect from the grid, and reconnect
with the real world.

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:59.350
This is something I've tried to incorporate
into my life as much as possible, but usually

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:01.080
is much harder than it should be.

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:05.600
The constant need to be online and in the
discussion, whatever that discussion is, can

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:11.149
be incredibly inspiring and valuable, but
it also can be draining and time sucking.

00:01:11.149 --> 00:01:15.119
Beyond just doing The Rubin Report, I've been
trying to work on a book for the past year,

00:01:15.119 --> 00:01:20.100
as well as catch up on a some side projects,
as well as seting a little time for mental

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:21.250
clarity.

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:24.380
With this in mind, I want to lay out the rest
of our summer for you:

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:28.509
This week on the show we have British columnist
and commentator Katie Hopkins, who is sure

00:01:28.509 --> 00:01:32.359
to trigger many of those who are trigger-able,
then I head to New York City to do The Greg

00:01:32.359 --> 00:01:34.630
Gutfeld Show.

00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:38.280
After this, I'll be truly experiencing one
of the highlights of my professional life

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:42.740
as I interview Richard Dawkins at the 92nd
Street Y in NYC.

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:46.600
The event sold out almost immediately before
I even had a chance to mention it to you guys,

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:52.990
but the fine folks at the Y are giving us
the video of the whole 2 hour interview, which

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:56.960
we'll be posting right here on our channel
next week.

00:01:56.960 --> 00:02:01.100
After this interview with Dawkins, I'll be
going off the grid completely for the rest

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:04.710
of the summer, until September 5th, which
the day after Labor day.

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:09.369
Fear not though, you will be getting new Rubin
Report episodes every week.

00:02:09.369 --> 00:02:13.830
We've already taped interviews with Professor
Gad Saad, columnist Guy Benson, economist

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:17.550
Pia Malaney, and chairman of the Ayn Rand
Institute, Yaron Brook.

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:21.070
Since we've taped these interviews already,
I can promise you you're gonna dig all of

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:24.710
them, and each episode is truly different
from each other.

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:29.020
What we may lose from filming and releasing
in the same week, I promise you get back with

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:33.700
a continued focus on ideas rather than news
cycles.

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:38.560
While we will post interviews as scheduled,
I will not be on social media of any kind

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:40.410
until September 5th.

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:46.840
That's right: I'm not going to tweet, post
on Facebook, share on Instagram, or anything

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:47.840
else.

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:50.890
We're going to automate some posts in advance
so we can promote our weekly episodes, but

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:55.250
I won't be sharing anything else, checking
mentions, or even reading the news.

00:02:55.250 --> 00:03:01.320
I'm looking forward to having some relaxation
time on the beach, but will spend most of

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:07.120
the this break catching up on reading, exercising,
and most importantly, focusing on this book,

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:08.150
which is long overdue.

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:11.910
Basically, I'm not going to look at screens
of any kind except for when I'm writing.

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:15.140
I'm sure people will try to talk to me about
the news, but I'm going do everything in my

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:19.540
power to truly shut down and really escape
from the day to day, play by play madness.

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:24.160
Yes, I'll miss some Trump tweets, I'll miss
a few faux outrages, and I'll miss whatever

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:28.290
else happens in the world, but I have a suspicion
that the world will keep spinning without

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:29.290
me.

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:33.360
And I also have a suspicion that I'll be better
off for this break afterwards.

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:37.610
It seems kinda crazy to take a vacation and
truly escape the web days, but that pretty

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:39.660
much was the norm only a decade ago.

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:43.880
If the world does end while I'm gone, I suppose
it'll have to end without me live-tweeting

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:44.880
it.

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:48.580
More importantly than anything else, I just
want to thank all of you who not only watch

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:53.050
this show, but share it with friends and family
and who are having these conversations in

00:03:53.050 --> 00:03:54.540
your own lives.

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:59.240
There is absolutely no doubt the issues we
are talking about here are taking root in

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:02.250
the real world and real change is on the horizon.

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:06.020
If I didn't think we could change the world
by having these honest conversations on the

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:11.650
importance of free speech and individual liberty,
I assure you I'd do something else.

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:14.910
It's never too late for me to pick up my NBA
dreams.

00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:18.489
Before I sign off, I want to give a special
shout out to all of you who have supported

00:04:18.489 --> 00:04:23.480
us on Patreon and PayPal since we went independent
about 14 months ago.

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:29.120
You guys truly have helped me make my dreams
come true and now you're giving me and my

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:33.240
crew a little breathing room, allowing me
to work on this book, and helping us take

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:35.050
it all to the next level.

00:04:35.050 --> 00:04:40.040
I already have a packed schedule of speaking
gigs and college events coming up this fall,

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:44.260
and I look forward to coming back more focused
and invigorated than ever before.

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:47.880
Without your support, not only couldn't we
do this show at the professional level which

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:52.210
we do it, but there's certainly no way I could
take a few weeks to clear the mind and plot

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:53.210
the future.

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:57.441
Maybe some of you will join me on this technology-free
couple weeks, but for those who don't, I know

00:04:57.441 --> 00:05:00.580
you'll enjoy everything we've cooked up for
you while I'm gone.

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:05.741
Again, thank you all for your support and
generosity and as we enter season 3 of The

00:05:05.741 --> 00:05:08.961
Rubin Report in September, I promise you,
this is just the beginning.

